format session-log-v1
stamp 20260821.215850
editor Claude Code
model claude-opus-5
voice Kyri
host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title The largest body the ladder ever measured, and the thirteen splits the lift opened
prompt Autonomous loop -- take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds, rota row per lap, condense REMEMBER when a set closes, send each increment
think Read Kyri and Radiant Style first, then the card. Standfast before anything: every living REDS row reads closed, and the one open item under %123 -- four cairns on no remote -- is explicitly Keaton's word, so it is a gate rather than agent-closable work. The line is clear to advance.
think The rota had no lap index recorded anywhere, since the grid was seated after the last two laps ran. Seated the convention rather than guessing each time: lap index counts session logs since the grid seated, so this is lap 2 and the row is Fire - Mars. Deep-read Standfast, reds-first, and the three depths of removal. Recorded here so the next lap reads row 3.
think Read the harness before the meter, as the arc's own teaching asks. The card named carry_the_amendment as next crux; the live meter named run_in_forbear at 10 rungs by 137 lines, 1,233 carried. The card was measured against a tree two lifts old, which is exactly the cohort-at-the-head-of-the-lap rule (REDS %111) working in reverse.
think Hashed every body by that name: ten texts, one hash, every one already public. The first family in this arc to stand whole with no absentee at all AND need no widening of its own name -- the cluster was written once, as one movement, and never touched.
think Read the reach closure before moving anything. Thirteen of the symbols it reaches stood private in all ten, so the fold widened them and lifted the body into ladder_checks.rye with the rung handed in comptime, every step reached as rung.step.
obs The meter caught my own incomplete work, and the number it printed was the tell. Carrying families rose 708 to 720 rather than falling to 707 -- thirteen more, exactly the count I had widened. Reading the scan's awk rather than assuming its key showed why: a family is keyed by its WHOLE body text, so pub fn x( and fn x( are two families. Widening ten members of a thirty-four-rung cohort split thirteen families by one word.
obs 84 lines of the reported fall were that artifact rather than any fold. A split family carries (copies-1) x lines twice instead of once, so splitting LOWERS measured carry while deduplicating nothing. The fall looked larger precisely because the work was less complete, which is the most dangerous shape a meter can take.
obs Healed it by widening each of the thirteen across its whole cohort -- seat_the_ground at forty-three, carry_the_amendment at thirty-six, read_the_appeal at twenty-nine. Families settled at 707, one fewer than before, and the carry fell 89,010 to 87,777: a fall of 1,233, exactly the family's own measured carry, with nothing borrowed.
obs The scan's own header already recorded a prior fold finding a family that differed in the word pub and nothing else. The lantern had fired once before; this lap it fired at me, from the same meter, in the same shape.
loom witness=caravan_ladder_carry carry_before=89010 carry_after=87777 fall=1233 families_before=708 families_split=720 families_after=707 ceiling=87800 modules=108 bodies=18122
loom witness=caravan_suite registered=105 green=105
file caravan/ladder_checks.rye the lifted body, 161 lines holding what ten rungs held apiece
file caravan/abate.rye one of the ten rungs whose copy left and whose call now names the harness
file caravan/ladder_checks.rye the reached steps stay each rung's own body; only the sequence lifts
file tools/caravan_ladder_carry_witness.rish the measured numbers, the new queue head, and the ceiling brought down
file tools/fixtures/caravan_ladder_carry_scan.sh the ceiling 89100 -> 87800
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge refreshed off measurement, the stale next-crux replaced by the one the meter names
recommend keep-going the next crux is measured and named -- seat_the_history at 17 rungs by 72 lines, with seat_the_record and main behind it. The rule this lap paid for rides with it: widen a word across the whole family it belongs to, never across the subset one lift happens to need.
